# A turn that stores a number into a slot of an object is laid out like any other: the list's kind and the counter's written bound are asked once, in front, also where the store stands in front of the read.
# A way out of a turn laid out is taken by running that turn again in the loop as written: so holes do not leave such turns, and a turn that something leaves behind its store (`leaves`) is not laid out.
# RUN: compile LoopsLaidOutWhoseTurnsStoreIntoSlots WrittenBoundsAskedOfListsInFrontOfTypedCopies mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic LoopsLaidOutWhoseTurnsStoreIntoSlots 2
# CHECK: statistic WrittenBoundsAskedOfListsInFrontOfTypedCopies 4
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: -630921332 40 -630921332 80 9 90
# RIGHT-NEXT: -1741656407 40 -1741656407 80 9 90
# RIGHT-NEXT: 1579574542 40 1579574542 80 9 90
# RIGHT-NEXT: 0 40 0 80 9 90
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
